  "title": "China AI Data Centre Boom Faces ROI Test",
  "lede": "A Goldman Sachs report finds China's AI data centre sector under growing pressure to demonstrate profitable returns as financing costs climb. The industry's focus is shifting away from rapid capacity buildout toward capital efficiency and strategies to improve investment returns. Japan is preparing a certification framework for data centres and cloud services aimed at reducing dependence on Chinese-linked infrastructure and supply chains. The scheme would allow the government to vet operators and steer sensitive workloads toward trusted providers. Singapore-based SC Capital Partners and South Korean AI cloud provider NeoAI Cloud have jointly invested in a 40MW AI data centre project in Pohang, South Korea. The project has also attracted government-backed capital, giving it public-sector support alongside private funding.",
